1
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:06,401
[This drama is intended for entertainment purposes only.]

2
00:00:06,411 --> 00:00:08,400
[All characters, behaviors, locations, and events depicted are fictional.]

3
00:00:08,430 --> 00:00:09,950
[It is not intended to be sexually suggestive or to encourage viewers]

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,501
[to engage in inappropriate or morally objectionable behavior.]

5
00:00:11,511 --> 00:00:12,890
[Nor is it intended to discredit any profession]

6
00:00:12,899 --> 00:00:13,900
[or create negative perceptions of any organization]

7
00:00:13,911 --> 00:00:14,912
[or any particular group of people.]

8
00:00:15,114 --> 00:00:19,270
Ma'am, someone sent us information about Hype Tech, the company
that won the smart card project.

9
00:00:19,278 --> 00:00:21,440
They have a history of colluding to rig government bids.

10
00:00:21,518 --> 00:00:24,120
If it's true, award the contract to the second-place bidder instead.

11
00:00:24,456 --> 00:00:27,720
Do you know that doll called Babina-Babini or something?

12
00:00:27,874 --> 00:00:31,360
- Bambinana?
- My daughter really wants one.

13
00:00:31,686 --> 00:00:34,640
I want a Bambinana doll with a red hat.

14
00:00:34,667 --> 00:00:36,720
And you'll have to line up. There are only a few available.

15
00:00:37,136 --> 00:00:40,000
Babe! Thank you so much.

16
00:00:40,010 --> 00:00:42,080
I don't think our relationship is healthy anymore.

17
00:00:42,224 --> 00:00:45,062
I've just been a little busy lately.

18
00:00:45,270 --> 00:00:47,920
- But…
- Honey, your coffee is getting cold.

19
00:00:48,352 --> 00:00:49,800
This is what I tried to tell you.

20
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:51,441
Goodbye, Nina.

21
00:00:51,646 --> 00:00:54,200
Jolene, you won't believe what just happened to me.

22
00:00:54,247 --> 00:00:58,248
Nopnapha called me in to sign the smart card project contract.

23
00:00:58,472 --> 00:01:01,560
Your plan worked. That company got kicked out,

24
00:01:01,580 --> 00:01:03,440
and we got the contract instead.

25
00:01:03,581 --> 00:01:07,400
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

26
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:10,261
Oh! The pretty sister is here!

27
00:01:16,342 --> 00:01:20,560
Mama Bear and Papa Bear fight and shout.

28
00:01:21,622 --> 00:01:26,040
Things break, and their voices thunder.

29
00:01:26,267 --> 00:01:28,200
Little Bear begins to cry,

30
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:31,960
his heart filled with fear.

31
00:01:33,806 --> 00:01:35,600
Will the sky come crashing

32
00:01:37,576 --> 00:01:38,920
down on him?

33
00:01:39,758 --> 00:01:42,280
Keep reading, Daddy.

34
00:01:49,539 --> 00:01:53,320
Little Bear trembles, scared out of his wits.

35
00:01:56,619 --> 00:02:01,520
He hides inside a hollow tree.

36
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:05,160
Keep reading, Daddy.

37
00:02:06,336 --> 00:02:09,080
Tetris, why aren't you asleep yet?

38
00:02:09,195 --> 00:02:11,800
Not yet, but Dad's already asleep.

39
00:02:13,616 --> 00:02:15,960
Honey? Honey!

40
00:02:19,307 --> 00:02:21,520
Oh, you're back.

41
00:02:23,211 --> 00:02:24,360
Where's Titus?

42
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:29,441
Sroi just took her to bed.

43
00:02:32,075 --> 00:02:33,120
Good, you're here.

44
00:02:33,366 --> 00:02:35,480
You can finish reading Tetris his bedtime story.

45
00:02:36,603 --> 00:02:38,790
Sweetie, Daddy's going to bed now.

46
00:02:46,126 --> 00:02:47,127
I'm off to bed.

47
00:02:54,611 --> 00:02:57,475
It's late, sweetheart. Daddy can finish the story tomorrow.

48
00:03:00,755 --> 00:03:04,360
Wow, that's beautiful! Who drew this?

49
00:03:04,406 --> 00:03:07,305
- I did.
- You drew this?

50
00:03:07,830 --> 00:03:11,360
Then why did you draw me wearing glasses? I don't wear glasses.

51
00:03:11,515 --> 00:03:14,520
That's not you, Mom. That's my teacher.

52
00:04:51,790 --> 00:04:53,240
Oh! The pretty sister is here!

53
00:04:53,536 --> 00:04:55,080
- See?
- We just talked about this.

54
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:12,481
Shit!

55
00:05:28,488 --> 00:05:29,840
Bambinana Red Hat!

56
00:05:45,411 --> 00:05:47,250
- Hi, Veekit.
- Hi.

57
00:05:47,931 --> 00:05:48,932
Where's Titus?

58
00:05:53,414 --> 00:05:54,800
Hey! Hey!

59
00:05:56,043 --> 00:05:59,960
Um, is that Bambinana Red Hat real?

60
00:06:00,486 --> 00:06:02,880
Of course. Do you collect them too?

61
00:06:03,334 --> 00:06:07,120
Yes! I have every version except that Red Hat one.

62
00:06:08,456 --> 00:06:10,136
Can I buy it from you?

63
00:06:13,475 --> 00:06:14,476
Sorry, sweetie. It's not for sale.

64
00:06:14,856 --> 00:06:17,480
My boyfriend bought it for me in America. It's special to me.

65
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:21,320
Please. I'm begging you.

66
00:06:21,424 --> 00:06:24,000
Name your price. I'll have my mom transfer the money right away.

67
00:06:24,283 --> 00:06:27,760
Please! I really want it for my birthday.

68
00:06:27,806 --> 00:06:30,475
Please sell it to me. I'm begging you.

69
00:06:30,480 --> 00:06:31,720
Is your birthday coming up?

70
00:06:32,280 --> 00:06:33,281
Yes.

71
00:06:35,304 --> 00:06:36,305
Well, then...

72
00:06:37,310 --> 00:06:40,200
I'll give it to you for free.

73
00:06:41,390 --> 00:06:43,720
But on one condition.

74
00:06:44,531 --> 00:06:47,600
Anything. Just tell me what you want. I'll do anything.

75
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:49,070
Can we be friends?

76
00:06:49,816 --> 00:06:52,400
Of course! I'm Titus. What's your name?

77
00:06:52,584 --> 00:06:53,585
I'm Ta.

78
00:06:55,107 --> 00:06:56,643
Happy birthday, Titus.

79
00:06:57,896 --> 00:06:59,395
Thank you, Ta.

80
00:07:02,747 --> 00:07:04,520
Now that we're friends,

81
00:07:05,059 --> 00:07:07,440
does that mean I'm invited to your birthday party?

82
00:07:07,907 --> 00:07:11,160
Of course. You'll be my VIP guest.

83
00:07:17,166 --> 00:07:18,167
Titus!

84
00:07:20,246 --> 00:07:21,247
Titus!

85
00:07:23,056 --> 00:07:24,680
Titus! Titus!

86
00:07:27,707 --> 00:07:28,708
Where have you been?

87
00:07:29,582 --> 00:07:32,451
A nice lady gave me a Bambinana Red Hat.

88
00:07:33,630 --> 00:07:36,206
She's so kind and really pretty.

89
00:07:36,430 --> 00:07:37,431
Isn't it cute?

90
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:40,401
Where is she?

91
00:07:40,611 --> 00:07:41,612
Over there.

92
00:07:45,395 --> 00:07:46,396
Huh? Where did she go?

93
00:07:49,700 --> 00:07:52,360
You little troublemaker. I bet you stole it from someone.

94
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:53,681
Causing trouble again, aren't you?

95
00:07:54,606 --> 00:07:57,607
I'm in a good mood today. I won't ruin it by yelling at you, you little queen.

96
00:07:58,974 --> 00:08:01,320
Hey! Where did you sneak off to without telling anyone?

97
00:08:01,598 --> 00:08:03,560
If you get kidnapped and sold off, don't expect me to rescue you.

98
00:08:24,904 --> 00:08:28,680
Everyone, this is Ta! She's my new friend!

99
00:08:28,987 --> 00:08:33,160
She gave me a limited-edition Bambinana Red Hat for my birthday!

100
00:08:34,558 --> 00:08:37,200
Ta is the kindest person in the whole world.

101
00:08:37,998 --> 00:08:41,499
From now on, whenever you and your friends do something fun,
don't forget to invite me.

102
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:44,041
Or I could help you with your homework.

103
00:08:44,050 --> 00:08:45,300
I'm really good at math and English.

104
00:08:47,910 --> 00:08:48,960
Isn't my cake gorgeous?

105
00:08:49,100 --> 00:08:52,160
- It's so pretty! I love eating here.
- Let's go!

106
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:56,760
- Come eat with us, Ta.
- Sure.

107
00:09:07,680 --> 00:09:09,280
It's a pleasure to be working with you.

108
00:09:11,798 --> 00:09:12,934
Likewise.

109
00:09:13,456 --> 00:09:15,040
I've been following your work for a long time.

110
00:09:15,147 --> 00:09:17,200
I'm so happy to have the chance to work with you.

111
00:09:17,648 --> 00:09:20,649
I'm happy to work with such a talented team too.

112
00:09:21,632 --> 00:09:23,520
Let's work together for our country.

113
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:25,041
Of course.

114
00:09:26,707 --> 00:09:29,454
And your other partner's name is...

115
00:09:30,856 --> 00:09:33,331
Nina. That's her nickname.

116
00:09:33,857 --> 00:09:34,858
Oh, Nina.

117
00:09:35,120 --> 00:09:36,560
Where is she?

118
00:09:37,910 --> 00:09:39,900
She's working in America.

119
00:09:40,118 --> 00:09:42,960
But she can work remotely from there. It's no problem.

120
00:09:44,064 --> 00:09:46,920
Young people really can work from anywhere these days.

121
00:09:47,288 --> 00:09:50,840
Some work together for years without ever meeting in person.

122
00:09:53,246 --> 00:09:55,522
Now that we're going to be working together,

123
00:09:55,966 --> 00:09:57,040
can I ask you something?

124
00:09:58,456 --> 00:09:59,457
Were you the one

125
00:10:00,440 --> 00:10:04,720
who tipped me off that Hype Tech had rigged bids before?

126
00:10:08,110 --> 00:10:09,843
Come on, admit it. I'm not upset.

127
00:10:10,776 --> 00:10:13,090
It's a good thing you dug that up.

128
00:10:13,886 --> 00:10:16,307
If the opposition had found out first, I'd be in serious trouble.

129
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:20,760
Yes. Munin was the one who dug up that information from the company.

130
00:10:22,160 --> 00:10:23,161
Munin?

131
00:10:24,918 --> 00:10:26,280
I mean Nina.

132
00:10:26,976 --> 00:10:30,064
Oh, isn't she working in America?

133
00:10:31,515 --> 00:10:34,394
She hacked into the company's system to get the information.

134
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:36,601
I see.

135
00:10:36,859 --> 00:10:38,700
Your friend is very talented.

136
00:10:39,070 --> 00:10:42,200
Let me know when she comes to Thailand. I'd love to invite her to dinner.

137
00:10:42,856 --> 00:10:43,857
Of course.

138
00:10:47,557 --> 00:10:48,558
Excuse me a moment.

139
00:10:51,539 --> 00:10:53,400
- What's up, sweetheart?
- Where are you, Mom?

140
00:10:53,659 --> 00:10:55,318
Mom, you have to come home right now.

141
00:10:55,451 --> 00:10:57,560
I'm at the Ministry. What's wrong, sweetheart?

142
00:10:57,792 --> 00:10:59,560
That homewrecking bitch has invaded our house, Mom.

143
00:10:59,702 --> 00:11:01,960
Who? Mutta?

144
00:11:02,224 --> 00:11:03,600
I don't know where Titus met her.

145
00:11:03,846 --> 00:11:05,334
But she invited her to her birthday party at our house.

146
00:11:07,526 --> 00:11:11,723
Napha, I bet Mutta deliberately got close to the kids.

147
00:11:12,032 --> 00:11:13,760
That bitch is more cunning than we thought.

148
00:11:14,187 --> 00:11:16,870
You need to get home and deal with her before she takes over our house.

149
00:11:17,680 --> 00:11:18,920
That bitch Mutta!

150
00:11:25,046 --> 00:11:26,960
One, two, cheese!

151
00:11:31,900 --> 00:11:32,901
Ta.

152
00:11:33,614 --> 00:11:34,615
Can I talk to you for a second?

153
00:11:35,518 --> 00:11:36,899
Dad, let's take a selfie.

154
00:11:38,456 --> 00:11:39,520
Come on, everyone. Get in.

155
00:11:41,739 --> 00:11:43,640
One, two, cheese!

156
00:11:47,558 --> 00:11:49,835
Titus, go play with your friends for a bit.

157
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:51,360
I need to talk to Ta privately.

158
00:11:52,112 --> 00:11:56,280
Don't take too long. Ta's my guest today, not yours.

159
00:11:57,771 --> 00:11:58,772
Okay, sweetie.

160
00:12:03,144 --> 00:12:05,160
What is it, Titus' dad?

161
00:12:07,864 --> 00:12:09,960
Let's talk inside. There are too many people here.

162
00:12:21,083 --> 00:12:22,160
How did you meet Titus?

163
00:12:23,435 --> 00:12:24,870
And why didn't you tell me you were coming today?

164
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:27,800
I wanted to surprise you.

165
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:31,400
Come on, Director. Smile.

166
00:12:31,699 --> 00:12:32,936
Why so serious?

167
00:12:33,763 --> 00:12:37,035
You should be happy I get along with your daughter.

168
00:12:37,528 --> 00:12:40,760
I'm going to be her mother someday, you know.

169
00:12:44,480 --> 00:12:47,707
I know, and I'm happy about that.

170
00:12:49,158 --> 00:12:50,360
But not today, Ta.

171
00:12:51,050 --> 00:12:52,880
Babe, please go home for now.

172
00:12:53,608 --> 00:12:56,320
If Napha comes home, all hell will break loose.

173
00:12:57,582 --> 00:13:00,240
I doubt she'd dare make a scene in front of the kids and parents

174
00:13:00,350 --> 00:13:02,200
at her own daughter's birthday party.

175
00:13:03,600 --> 00:13:04,601
You never know.

176
00:13:07,107 --> 00:13:08,800
We know you're here to cause trouble.

177
00:13:09,320 --> 00:13:11,160
How many times have you tried to provoke Aunt Napha?

178
00:13:11,635 --> 00:13:14,051
It won't work this time. Just go home.

179
00:13:14,110 --> 00:13:17,539
Hey, Veekit. This is none of your business.

180
00:13:18,227 --> 00:13:20,320
Go somewhere else. I'll handle this myself.

181
00:13:20,830 --> 00:13:22,958
You? What can you possibly do?

182
00:13:23,731 --> 00:13:25,320
Ta's more likely to get the better of you.

183
00:13:25,987 --> 00:13:27,806
And Aunt Napha might come after you too.

184
00:13:28,083 --> 00:13:29,084
Veekit!

185
00:13:30,606 --> 00:13:33,080
Ta! Veekit! Let's play hide-and-seek! Come on!

186
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:36,600
Come on, Ta! Hurry!

187
00:13:44,085 --> 00:13:45,500
So how exactly are you going to handle this?

188
00:13:46,659 --> 00:13:47,660
I don't know, damn it!

189
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:51,000
Let's just let them play for a while.

190
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:52,680
I'll take Ta home myself.

191
00:13:53,832 --> 00:13:55,200
Napha probably won't be back until this evening.

192
00:13:56,547 --> 00:13:58,080
Hurry up, Veekit.

193
00:14:06,678 --> 00:14:08,360
Rock, paper, scissors!

194
00:14:09,718 --> 00:14:11,170
Rock, paper, scissors!

195
00:14:12,803 --> 00:14:14,300
Rock, paper, scissors!

196
00:14:14,804 --> 00:14:17,300
How about this? I'll volunteer to be the seeker first.

197
00:14:19,955 --> 00:14:21,401
Okay, let's start.

198
00:14:22,027 --> 00:14:23,028
I'm going to count now.

199
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:24,481
One.

200
00:14:25,179 --> 00:14:26,180
Two.

201
00:14:27,180 --> 00:14:28,181
Three.

202
00:14:29,067 --> 00:14:31,400
Four, five, six, seven.

203
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:33,201
Eight.

204
00:14:33,720 --> 00:14:34,721
Nine.

205
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:36,321
Ten.

206
00:14:38,894 --> 00:14:41,040
Ta, let's hide behind the bed in my room.

207
00:14:41,091 --> 00:14:43,280
- I bet Veekit will never find us. Come on.
- Wait, Titus.

208
00:14:43,971 --> 00:14:45,464
If we hide together,

209
00:14:45,838 --> 00:14:48,165
we'll both get caught at the same time.

210
00:14:48,664 --> 00:14:50,040
I think we should hide separately.

211
00:14:52,555 --> 00:14:53,556
What's that room?

212
00:14:53,792 --> 00:14:56,120
That's Tetris's room. Better stay out of there.

213
00:14:56,251 --> 00:14:57,280
Or they'll make a fuss again.

214
00:14:58,107 --> 00:14:59,108
Then...

215
00:15:00,198 --> 00:15:02,300
- What about that room?
- That's Mom's room.

216
00:15:03,691 --> 00:15:06,240
Oh, but you can hide in the prayer room!

217
00:15:06,358 --> 00:15:08,880
There's a hiding spot under the altar table. It's over there.

218
00:15:09,243 --> 00:15:11,044
- Okay, I'll hide in the prayer room.
- Okay!

219
00:16:17,637 --> 00:16:20,120
They use burner phones to arrange their jobs.

220
00:16:20,616 --> 00:16:22,040
Once the job's done, they crush the phones and throw them away.

221
00:16:22,867 --> 00:16:24,440
You'll never be able to track any of them down.

222
00:16:38,868 --> 00:16:39,869
Napha!

223
00:16:40,952 --> 00:16:42,453
Why are you home so early?

224
00:16:42,878 --> 00:16:44,250
Because termites have invaded my house.

225
00:16:44,798 --> 00:16:47,840
Am I supposed to wait until they bring the whole house down?
I have to get rid of them!

226
00:16:48,072 --> 00:16:49,073
Where is she?

227
00:16:49,123 --> 00:16:50,936
- Where's that queen termite?
- Calm down, Napha.

228
00:16:51,198 --> 00:16:53,320
- Where is she?
- She's playing hide-and-seek, Mom.

229
00:16:53,422 --> 00:16:55,600
- I saw Titus take her inside to hide.
- Tetris!

230
00:16:56,798 --> 00:16:59,000
Napha, the house is full of guests.

231
00:16:59,240 --> 00:17:00,600
Can we please not make a scene today?

232
00:17:01,246 --> 00:17:03,720
That homewrecking bitch has the nerve to come into my home!

233
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:05,560
If I don't confront her now, when should I?

234
00:17:05,570 --> 00:17:07,720
Keep your voice down, Napha.

235
00:17:09,470 --> 00:17:11,520
Hello, ma'am.

236
00:17:12,531 --> 00:17:13,532
Hello.

237
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:17,160
How's the food? Is it good?

238
00:17:17,577 --> 00:17:21,200
It's delicious. And all the desserts are from famous shops.

239
00:17:21,795 --> 00:17:23,360
I picked them out especially for you.

240
00:17:24,544 --> 00:17:26,560
Please enjoy yourselves. Excuse me.

241
00:17:27,568 --> 00:17:32,169
Ma'am, we were just discussing the parent-teacher association.

242
00:17:32,443 --> 00:17:34,720
There's a project we'd love your support with.

243
00:17:36,286 --> 00:17:38,240
You can discuss it with Director Jenphop.

244
00:17:39,571 --> 00:17:40,672
Stay with Daddy, Tetris.

245
00:17:44,572 --> 00:17:45,573
Director?

246
00:17:46,600 --> 00:17:47,601
Right this way, please.

247
00:17:47,952 --> 00:17:49,520
Honestly, these people!

248
00:17:49,776 --> 00:17:53,360
The moment they see I'm a minister, they start sucking up to me.

249
00:17:59,963 --> 00:18:03,040
Slap that bitch, Mom. Give her one for me too.

250
00:18:29,832 --> 00:18:30,833
You bitch, Mutta!

251
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:01,001
- Gotcha!
- Oh!

252
00:19:04,350 --> 00:19:05,720
You can't catch me, ma'am.

253
00:19:07,150 --> 00:19:10,500
Mutta! How dare you barge into my bedroom!

254
00:19:10,974 --> 00:19:11,975
Get out!

255
00:19:13,667 --> 00:19:14,760
It's your bedroom today.

256
00:19:15,246 --> 00:19:18,040
But who knows? It might be mine someday.

257
00:19:18,752 --> 00:19:19,753
Or...

258
00:19:20,078 --> 00:19:21,840
Would you rather I share a bedroom with the Director?

259
00:19:22,320 --> 00:19:23,321
Come here!

260
00:19:23,654 --> 00:19:25,920
I won't let you contaminate my room with your filth.

261
00:19:26,515 --> 00:19:27,800
This room is no place for you.

262
00:19:27,998 --> 00:19:29,672
Come here! Get over here!

263
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:32,640
This is a limited edition. It's really hard to find.

264
00:19:32,750 --> 00:19:35,640
But Ta managed to get one for me. Isn't she amazing?

265
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,301
Come join your friends over here.

266
00:19:39,904 --> 00:19:40,905
Let's see.

267
00:19:41,638 --> 00:19:43,000
Is everyone here? Are we missing anyone?

268
00:19:43,558 --> 00:19:46,363
Ta's missing. You'll never find her! Ah!

269
00:19:48,912 --> 00:19:51,360
And my little sister, Kambum, too.

270
00:19:56,347 --> 00:19:57,348
Come here!

271
00:19:58,971 --> 00:20:02,400
Tell me! What are you trying to destroy in my family?

272
00:20:03,067 --> 00:20:04,768
I don't have to lift a finger.

273
00:20:05,430 --> 00:20:08,300
Your family's already falling apart, isn't it?

274
00:20:09,031 --> 00:20:11,400
Would it be falling apart if it weren't for a termite like you?

275
00:20:14,384 --> 00:20:17,640
Let me tell you something. I've been very merciful to you.

276
00:20:17,974 --> 00:20:20,600
I've let you live your shameless life this long.

277
00:20:20,886 --> 00:20:24,120
Ever heard of a fatal bloodstream infection?

278
00:20:24,886 --> 00:20:26,120
Being burned alive inside a tire?

279
00:20:27,072 --> 00:20:28,073
Being thrown into a river with weights tied to you?

280
00:20:29,254 --> 00:20:31,040
Take your pick. How do you want to die?

281
00:20:31,627 --> 00:20:34,454
You dare talk about such evil things in front of Buddha?

282
00:20:35,456 --> 00:20:38,480
You must know what a terrible sinner you are.

283
00:20:38,987 --> 00:20:41,080
That's why you built such a huge prayer room.

284
00:20:41,766 --> 00:20:43,040
Let me tell you something.

285
00:20:43,483 --> 00:20:45,640
Even if you built a giant pagoda over your house,

286
00:20:45,872 --> 00:20:46,920
you'd never escape me.

287
00:20:47,648 --> 00:20:50,360
I'll haunt you like a ghost,

288
00:20:50,800 --> 00:20:52,840
until you finally get what you deserve.

289
00:20:53,824 --> 00:20:54,880
If you're a ghost,

290
00:20:55,936 --> 00:20:58,037
then I'll be the exorcist who gets rid of you!

291
00:21:01,136 --> 00:21:04,267
May the Buddha, Dharma, and Sangha protect me.

292
00:21:04,736 --> 00:21:08,400
May all evil spirits who wish me harm vanish.

293
00:21:17,470 --> 00:21:19,720
You wandering spirit! You filthy whore!

294
00:21:19,784 --> 00:21:21,280
Get the hell out of my house! Now!

295
00:21:21,795 --> 00:21:23,950
You can splash holy water on me all you want.

296
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:25,001
I'll just get wet.

297
00:21:25,171 --> 00:21:27,880
But you can't kick me out! Is this even your house?

298
00:21:28,056 --> 00:21:29,157
It's the Director's house.

299
00:21:29,363 --> 00:21:31,160
The reason he never wants to come home after work

300
00:21:31,262 --> 00:21:33,680
is because seeing your face is like seeing a ghost.

301
00:21:33,814 --> 00:21:36,040
You're the one who needs to leave!

302
00:21:44,803 --> 00:21:47,600
Jenphop may have built this house,

303
00:21:47,875 --> 00:21:49,920
but it's on my land.

304
00:21:50,238 --> 00:21:51,923
And the title deed is in my name.

305
00:21:52,040 --> 00:21:53,480
Get that through your thick skull, you idiot.

306
00:21:54,024 --> 00:21:55,325
Trying to run away from me? Come here.

307
00:21:55,678 --> 00:21:56,679
Get over here.

308
00:21:57,891 --> 00:21:59,840
Just die already, you bitch from hell.

309
00:22:15,840 --> 00:22:16,841
Bye-bye!

310
00:22:17,232 --> 00:22:20,160
- Goodbye!
- Goodbye!

311
00:22:20,320 --> 00:22:22,440
- Come again!
- Thank you, sweetheart!

312
00:22:22,606 --> 00:22:24,840
- Goodbye!
- Goodbye!

313
00:22:28,126 --> 00:22:30,040
Please come to Kampaong and Kambum's birthday party.

314
00:22:30,100 --> 00:22:32,080
You and Titus are both invited.

315
00:22:32,232 --> 00:22:33,133
Of course.

316
00:22:33,192 --> 00:22:35,880
- We'll be going now. Goodbye.
- Goodbye!

317
00:22:35,987 --> 00:22:37,288
Kambum, say goodbye to the Minister, sweetie.

318
00:22:37,486 --> 00:22:38,487
Come on, say goodbye.

319
00:22:42,400 --> 00:22:44,440
Oh, I'm sorry. I should get going.

320
00:22:47,046 --> 00:22:48,047
What's the matter with her?

321
00:22:48,470 --> 00:22:53,040
Mom, what's wrong with her? Why did she cry so much when she saw you?

322
00:22:54,131 --> 00:22:57,571
She was probably... sleepy, sweetheart. That's why she was fussy.

323
00:23:02,320 --> 00:23:05,480
Ta, what happened? Why are you all wet?

324
00:23:06,614 --> 00:23:09,440
I ran into a ghost, so I washed myself with holy water.

325
00:23:09,776 --> 00:23:11,640
This house is seriously haunted.

326
00:23:14,432 --> 00:23:16,795
But are you leaving already, Ta?

327
00:23:16,934 --> 00:23:21,450
Stay for dinner with us! Please? Pretty please?

328
00:23:21,520 --> 00:23:24,280
Let her go. She has things to take care of.

329
00:23:25,344 --> 00:23:26,345
Right?

330
00:23:28,038 --> 00:23:31,800
Your house is beautiful, ma'am. So lush and peaceful.

331
00:23:32,518 --> 00:23:33,519
It must be lovely to live here.

332
00:23:34,800 --> 00:23:36,600
Can I come visit more often?

333
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:38,301
Of course.

334
00:23:38,486 --> 00:23:41,520
You're welcome anytime, Ta. Don't be shy.

335
00:23:42,528 --> 00:23:43,529
Well, then...

336
00:23:44,427 --> 00:23:46,028
I'll be going now, ma'am.

337
00:23:47,723 --> 00:23:49,611
See you at the Ministry, Director.

338
00:23:50,939 --> 00:23:51,940
See you, Veekit.

339
00:23:59,355 --> 00:24:00,760
I'll walk Ta to her car.

340
00:24:04,776 --> 00:24:06,611
I'll come too.

341
00:24:06,800 --> 00:24:07,801
No need.

342
00:24:08,360 --> 00:24:09,661
We need to talk.

343
00:24:14,912 --> 00:24:17,419
I'm ordering you to stay away from that bitch Mutta.

344
00:24:18,422 --> 00:24:20,464
Don't ask questions. That's an order.

345
00:24:21,000 --> 00:24:22,101
Just do as I say.

346
00:24:22,624 --> 00:24:25,400
If you don't give me a reason, I won't do it.

347
00:24:27,254 --> 00:24:28,928
Since when did you stop listening to me, Titus?

348
00:24:29,419 --> 00:24:31,800
A long time ago. You only just noticed?

349
00:24:32,235 --> 00:24:33,615
She's your father's mistress.

350
00:24:34,195 --> 00:24:35,896
You can't be friends with your father's mistress!

351
00:24:38,888 --> 00:24:42,360
That's not true! Ta said she works with Dad at the Ministry.

352
00:24:42,616 --> 00:24:44,400
She never said she was Dad's mistress.

353
00:24:45,352 --> 00:24:46,353
Right?

354
00:24:47,353 --> 00:24:48,354
Uh...

355
00:24:49,500 --> 00:24:51,501
Just do what Mom said.

356
00:24:51,635 --> 00:24:53,260
Listen to your mom, Titus.

357
00:24:53,651 --> 00:24:56,648
Besides, you're still young. Let the adults handle this.

358
00:24:57,000 --> 00:24:58,995
Tetris, don't bring this up again.

359
00:25:02,822 --> 00:25:04,747
But I want Ta to be Dad's mistress!

360
00:25:05,574 --> 00:25:08,360
Oh my God, Titus! How can you say that?

361
00:25:09,900 --> 00:25:11,801
Ta gave me a Bambinana.

362
00:25:12,160 --> 00:25:13,915
She came to my birthday party.

363
00:25:14,459 --> 00:25:17,515
She talks to me every day and always replies to my messages.

364
00:25:17,883 --> 00:25:18,884
Unlike you.

365
00:25:19,456 --> 00:25:21,320
You never do anything for me.

366
00:25:21,531 --> 00:25:22,532
Titus!

367
00:25:23,211 --> 00:25:25,227
But Mom gave birth to us.

368
00:25:25,638 --> 00:25:29,520
You'll hurt her feelings if you say things like that, you know?

369
00:25:30,070 --> 00:25:31,200
Apologize to your mother right now.

370
00:25:31,782 --> 00:25:32,783
No!

371
00:25:33,702 --> 00:25:36,760
I want Ta to be my mom! I want Ta to be my mom!

372
00:25:38,064 --> 00:25:40,640
I didn't teach her to say that.

373
00:25:40,883 --> 00:25:41,884
She said it on her own.

374
00:25:46,947 --> 00:25:48,640
You want that bitch to be your mother so badly?

375
00:25:57,320 --> 00:25:59,221
You want that bitch to be your mother so badly?

376
00:25:59,923 --> 00:26:00,924
Yes!

377
00:26:02,110 --> 00:26:03,111
Fine!

378
00:26:04,163 --> 00:26:05,640
- Give me that!
- Auntie!

379
00:26:06,264 --> 00:26:08,440
- Auntie!
- Give me back my stuff!

380
00:26:11,240 --> 00:26:12,920
You want that bitch to be your mother so badly?

381
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:14,301
Mom, give it back!

382
00:26:14,867 --> 00:26:16,320
Just die already, you damn banana!

383
00:26:16,643 --> 00:26:17,644
- Mom!
- Napha!

384
00:26:42,659 --> 00:26:45,280
This is what I'll use to prove

385
00:26:45,448 --> 00:26:47,000
that Nopnapha ordered my sister's murder.

386
00:26:50,040 --> 00:26:52,920
It's just a burner phone. Anyone could have one.

387
00:26:53,541 --> 00:26:56,300
The court won't accept that alone as evidence.

388
00:26:57,123 --> 00:26:58,371
I'll find more evidence.

389
00:26:58,942 --> 00:27:00,840
We need several pieces of evidence to build a solid case,

390
00:27:00,872 --> 00:27:01,960
so she won't be able to get away with it.

391
00:27:02,334 --> 00:27:05,040
I've already gotten close to her younger child.

392
00:27:05,560 --> 00:27:07,761
Now I'll find a way to get close to the older one.

393
00:27:08,014 --> 00:27:09,615
I'm sure I'll uncover plenty more useful information.

394
00:27:11,491 --> 00:27:12,492
Oh, Munin.

395
00:27:13,336 --> 00:27:15,918
I signed the Smart Card project contract today.

396
00:27:16,840 --> 00:27:20,910
If we pull this off, it'll be a huge boost to our company's reputation.

397
00:27:21,736 --> 00:27:24,835
I know. That's why I got you to submit a bid.

398
00:27:27,347 --> 00:27:30,718
But weren't you planning to sabotage the project
to ruin Nopnapha's reputation?

399
00:27:32,000 --> 00:27:33,001
Munin.

400
00:27:33,601 --> 00:27:36,760
If she goes down, we go down with her.

401
00:27:38,602 --> 00:27:40,163
Can't you go after her for something else?

402
00:27:41,120 --> 00:27:43,595
Just leave our project out of it. Please.

403
00:27:46,219 --> 00:27:48,300
Okay, fine.

404
00:27:50,352 --> 00:27:53,552
I promise I won't put our company at risk.

405
00:27:55,152 --> 00:27:56,880
But you have to help me take her down.

406
00:27:57,768 --> 00:27:59,816
Don't you have a friend in forensic science?

407
00:28:01,160 --> 00:28:04,000
Get this phone checked for Nopnapha's fingerprints.

408
00:28:36,400 --> 00:28:37,801
It's jasmine-scented, Mom.

409
00:28:38,400 --> 00:28:41,160
Perfect for a senior citizen like you.

410
00:28:43,842 --> 00:28:45,443
I'm a minister, sweetheart.

411
00:28:46,486 --> 00:28:48,200
Oh, right, Mom.

412
00:28:49,579 --> 00:28:50,800
But it smells lovely, Tetris.

413
00:28:52,798 --> 00:28:55,920
Tetris, thank you for being such a good kid.

414
00:28:56,163 --> 00:28:57,600
And not giving you any headaches.

415
00:28:59,320 --> 00:29:02,120
I know

416
00:29:02,483 --> 00:29:04,484
you have so much to deal with every day.

417
00:29:07,987 --> 00:29:10,504
If there's anything I can do to help, just tell me.

418
00:29:11,384 --> 00:29:13,080
You're the sweetest, darling.

419
00:29:15,792 --> 00:29:16,793
Thank you.

420
00:29:21,056 --> 00:29:22,057
It smells lovely.

421
00:29:23,600 --> 00:29:24,601
It's me.

422
00:29:25,088 --> 00:29:26,089
Yes?

423
00:29:28,112 --> 00:29:29,113
Auntie,

424
00:29:29,819 --> 00:29:31,504
I think you should go talk to Titus.

425
00:29:32,710 --> 00:29:33,880
She seems really upset.

426
00:29:35,422 --> 00:29:38,320
She's locked herself in her room and won't answer when I call.

427
00:29:39,246 --> 00:29:40,723
Forget that drama queen, Veekit.

428
00:29:41,358 --> 00:29:42,803
She'll come out when she gets hungry.

429
00:29:44,600 --> 00:29:45,640
I'll talk to her tomorrow.

430
00:29:46,622 --> 00:29:48,259
For now, let her think about what she's done.

431
00:29:48,691 --> 00:29:49,720
Off to bed, everyone. Go on.

432
00:29:52,366 --> 00:29:53,800
Who put it here?

433
00:30:21,798 --> 00:30:22,960
Wait, Auntie.

434
00:30:25,600 --> 00:30:26,601
Auntie!

435
00:30:27,101 --> 00:30:29,275
If you scold Titus now, it'll only make things worse.

436
00:30:31,158 --> 00:30:33,000
Why don't you try talking to her calmly?

437
00:30:46,659 --> 00:30:47,660
Titus!

438
00:30:49,331 --> 00:30:51,075
Open the door. I want to talk to you.

439
00:30:57,294 --> 00:30:59,944
If you don't answer, I'm unlocking the door.

440
00:31:03,715 --> 00:31:04,716
Give me the key.

441
00:31:09,920 --> 00:31:10,921
Titus!

442
00:31:28,928 --> 00:31:29,929
Auntie.

443
00:31:34,075 --> 00:31:36,416
I hate Mom! I want a new mom!

444
00:31:47,800 --> 00:31:48,801
Titus.

445
00:31:49,280 --> 00:31:50,294
Come on, tell me.

446
00:31:50,848 --> 00:31:52,560
Did you tell Mom and Dad you were going out?

447
00:31:54,352 --> 00:31:56,758
Why should I have to tell anyone?

448
00:31:57,040 --> 00:31:58,600
I have you as my other mom now.

449
00:31:59,041 --> 00:32:00,042
My second mom.

450
00:32:00,422 --> 00:32:02,800
Huh? What do you mean, second mom?

451
00:32:05,224 --> 00:32:07,624
Well, you're Dad's mistress.

452
00:32:08,376 --> 00:32:09,464
So that makes you my second mom.

453
00:32:14,040 --> 00:32:15,760
If I really were your mom,

454
00:32:16,800 --> 00:32:18,520
which mom would you love more?

455
00:32:18,984 --> 00:32:21,800
Nopnapha or Mutta?

456
00:32:22,915 --> 00:32:24,886
Mutta, of course!

457
00:32:25,200 --> 00:32:27,520
I'd even stop being Nopnapha's daughter.

458
00:32:31,195 --> 00:32:33,480
I'm happy you love me, Titus.

459
00:32:33,960 --> 00:32:37,150
But your mom and dad are still married.

460
00:32:37,518 --> 00:32:39,200
So I can't be your other mom.

461
00:32:40,227 --> 00:32:42,688
Hurry up and eat. Then I'll call your dad to pick you up.

462
00:32:43,840 --> 00:32:45,860
No! I'm not going home!

463
00:32:45,886 --> 00:32:47,560
Can I stay with you, Ta?

464
00:32:47,600 --> 00:32:49,960
I don't want to see Mom.

465
00:32:50,001 --> 00:32:51,680
- Please! I don't want to go home!
- Okay, okay. You don't have to.

466
00:32:52,638 --> 00:32:54,160
But I need to call Veekit.

467
00:32:54,752 --> 00:32:57,387
Your family needs to know you're here, or they'll worry.

468
00:33:08,598 --> 00:33:10,944
Hello, Ta. I was just about to call you.

469
00:33:14,112 --> 00:33:15,158
Is Titus with you?

470
00:33:15,819 --> 00:33:17,760
Yeah, she's with me.

471
00:33:17,915 --> 00:33:20,075
Tell everyone not to worry. She's safe.

472
00:33:22,560 --> 00:33:24,960
Titus is with Ta. She's safe.

473
00:33:25,880 --> 00:33:27,200
- Give me that. I'll talk to her.
- Ta!

474
00:33:27,300 --> 00:33:29,840
Can you calm down? Let me handle this.

475
00:33:32,582 --> 00:33:33,720
What did she say?

476
00:33:34,139 --> 00:33:35,520
She refuses to go home.

477
00:33:36,100 --> 00:33:38,560
Can you come talk to her? I don't know what else to say.

478
00:33:39,286 --> 00:33:41,579
Okay. Look after her until I get there.

479
00:33:42,043 --> 00:33:43,744
Just keep her company and talk about anything.

480
00:33:43,800 --> 00:33:46,318
But don't scold her, criticize her, or lecture her.

481
00:33:46,520 --> 00:33:47,521
That'll only make things worse.

482
00:33:48,056 --> 00:33:49,057
I'll be there as soon as I can.

483
00:33:54,755 --> 00:33:56,360
I'll go see Titus at Ta's condo.

484
00:33:57,683 --> 00:33:59,240
Make sure you bring her home.

485
00:33:59,710 --> 00:34:02,800
If that woman refuses to let her go, we'll call the police.

486
00:34:02,900 --> 00:34:05,901
Mom, Titus went to Ta on her own.

487
00:34:06,101 --> 00:34:08,238
And Ta asked me to come help talk her into coming home.

488
00:34:09,214 --> 00:34:11,251
Can you all stop assuming the worst about Ta?

489
00:34:13,358 --> 00:34:15,059
I'll let you know as soon as I hear anything.

490
00:34:20,949 --> 00:34:22,812
This is all your fault!

491
00:34:23,851 --> 00:34:25,840
You knew Titus was already upset with you.

492
00:34:26,358 --> 00:34:28,800
- And you still went and chopped up her banana doll!
- Dad!

493
00:34:29,691 --> 00:34:31,760
Didn't this whole mess start because you have a mistress?

494
00:34:32,310 --> 00:34:33,520
Why are you blaming Mom?

495
00:34:33,893 --> 00:34:34,694
Tetris!

496
00:34:34,728 --> 00:34:38,760
Even the kids know who's responsible

497
00:34:39,046 --> 00:34:41,677
for all the chaos in this family. Wake up, Phop!

498
00:34:41,838 --> 00:34:43,560
And start changing your ways!

499
00:34:44,227 --> 00:34:45,228
Exactly!

500
00:34:46,054 --> 00:34:48,112
Try to leave your children something to respect you for.

501
00:34:51,515 --> 00:34:52,886
Break up with that woman right now,

502
00:34:53,500 --> 00:34:55,501
before our family falls apart completely.

503
00:34:58,301 --> 00:35:00,000
Now you're all ganging up on me!

504
00:35:00,531 --> 00:35:01,720
Nobody's going anywhere.

505
00:35:02,678 --> 00:35:04,880
We're all staying here until Titus comes home.

506
00:35:11,163 --> 00:35:14,880
- No! I'm not going back! Let me go!
- Titus, calm down. Just listen to me!

507
00:35:14,910 --> 00:35:18,240
I won't listen! You're on Mom's side anyway! Get out!

508
00:35:18,700 --> 00:35:19,744
Titus!

509
00:35:19,856 --> 00:35:22,000
I want to stay with Ta! I told you to go home!

510
00:35:22,057 --> 00:35:24,470
- I'm not going back! I'm staying with Ta! Just go home!
- Titus!

511
00:35:24,500 --> 00:35:25,501
I'm not going back.

512
00:35:25,550 --> 00:35:26,551
Titus.

513
00:35:27,326 --> 00:35:28,960
Do you still want to be friends with me?

514
00:35:30,800 --> 00:35:32,120
Of course.

515
00:35:34,352 --> 00:35:35,880
But if you don't go home,

516
00:35:36,592 --> 00:35:40,760
your mom will get even angrier with me and
blame me for making you disobedient.

517
00:35:41,334 --> 00:35:44,294
She might even call the police and have me arrested.

518
00:35:44,896 --> 00:35:46,086
Because you're still a child,

519
00:35:46,592 --> 00:35:49,440
you can't stay at someone else's home without your parents' permission.

520
00:35:50,811 --> 00:35:52,360
And if things get that serious,

521
00:35:53,414 --> 00:35:54,680
we might never see each other again.

522
00:35:57,739 --> 00:36:01,640
But I really don't want to go home.

523
00:36:05,837 --> 00:36:06,838
How about this?

524
00:36:08,366 --> 00:36:11,320
Why don't you stay here with me for one night?

525
00:36:12,344 --> 00:36:13,645
Then you can go home tomorrow.

526
00:36:14,774 --> 00:36:16,440
And when you get home, tell your mom

527
00:36:16,700 --> 00:36:18,760
you'd like to come visit me more often.

528
00:36:18,849 --> 00:36:20,480
Because you love me.

529
00:36:20,850 --> 00:36:25,320
If you ask her nicely, I'm sure she'll say yes. Right?

530
00:36:37,801 --> 00:36:39,464
Can't she just go home tonight?

531
00:36:42,182 --> 00:36:44,224
Okay, let's do that then.

532
00:36:45,798 --> 00:36:46,799
Please take care of her.

533
00:36:50,486 --> 00:36:51,487
That bitch!

534
00:36:51,811 --> 00:36:54,640
It's not enough that she seduces men. Now she's manipulating a child too!

535
00:36:55,200 --> 00:36:56,835
What's wrong? What did Veekit say?

536
00:36:58,670 --> 00:36:59,671
Veekit said

537
00:37:00,256 --> 00:37:02,520
Titus wants to stay there tonight and come home tomorrow.

538
00:37:03,019 --> 00:37:04,544
And Veekit will stay there to look after her.

539
00:37:05,120 --> 00:37:07,121
Oh, no way!

540
00:37:07,456 --> 00:37:09,926
That bitch is definitely going to seduce Veekit! I won't allow it!

541
00:37:10,923 --> 00:37:13,960
That's true! Every man who gets close to her falls into her trap!

542
00:37:14,198 --> 00:37:16,784
Napha, let's take the police to her condo

543
00:37:16,838 --> 00:37:18,440
and rescue Titus and Veekit.

544
00:37:19,456 --> 00:37:21,960
Veekit said Titus refuses to come home no matter what he says.

545
00:37:22,208 --> 00:37:24,320
Forcing her will only make things worse.

546
00:37:26,395 --> 00:37:28,651
I'm sure that bitch planned this whole thing.

547
00:37:29,110 --> 00:37:30,800
I'd love to drag her out and beat the hell out of her.

548
00:37:30,840 --> 00:37:31,841
Okay, how about this?

549
00:37:34,840 --> 00:37:37,864
I'll go stay with Titus and send Veekit home.

550
00:37:39,102 --> 00:37:40,103
Not a chance!

551
00:37:41,027 --> 00:37:42,560
You're just taking advantage of the situation.

552
00:37:43,387 --> 00:37:46,720
If you go, your daughter will come home alone in a taxi tomorrow,

553
00:37:46,944 --> 00:37:48,688
while you'll be in bed with that woman all day and night.

554
00:37:49,280 --> 00:37:52,123
Hey, but what if Veekit falls for her tricks?

555
00:37:52,896 --> 00:37:57,120
Our family will lose two good men to the same woman.

556
00:37:57,584 --> 00:37:59,560
There won't be any men left in our family.

557
00:38:05,086 --> 00:38:06,320
I trust Veekit.

558
00:38:08,051 --> 00:38:11,960
He wouldn't be blinded by lust like Phop.

559
00:38:22,221 --> 00:38:24,720
Watch out for that bitch, Veekit. I'm worried about you.

560
00:38:27,131 --> 00:38:30,400
Don't worry. I can handle myself. Go to bed.

561
00:38:44,165 --> 00:38:45,200
How's Titus?

562
00:38:46,640 --> 00:38:47,641
She's asleep.

563
00:38:49,140 --> 00:38:50,518
You're pretty good with kids, aren't you?

564
00:38:53,465 --> 00:38:54,819
You mean I'm good at manipulating them?

565
00:38:56,467 --> 00:38:57,640
You're good at manipulating adults too.

566
00:38:58,982 --> 00:39:02,200
But you're a magician. Aren't you better at fooling people?

567
00:39:04,352 --> 00:39:06,491
Magicians aren't con artists, you know.

568
00:39:08,019 --> 00:39:09,760
We don't hide the truth from anyone.

569
00:39:17,048 --> 00:39:19,249
The audience knows they're watching an illusion.

570
00:39:30,659 --> 00:39:32,240
They know they're being fooled by a trick.

571
00:39:48,613 --> 00:39:49,680
But con artists

572
00:39:50,880 --> 00:39:52,805
mix the truth with lies.

573
00:39:54,294 --> 00:39:55,824
Until you can't tell them apart.

574
00:39:58,038 --> 00:39:59,680
The people being deceived often don't even realize it.

575
00:40:01,397 --> 00:40:04,860
And sometimes, even when someone's sitting right in front of us,

576
00:40:06,183 --> 00:40:07,500
we still have no idea

577
00:40:09,431 --> 00:40:11,520
who they really are.

578
00:40:14,749 --> 00:40:16,886
When you watch other magicians perform,

579
00:40:17,846 --> 00:40:19,250
can you ever figure out their tricks?

580
00:40:22,187 --> 00:40:23,188
Of course.

581
00:40:24,288 --> 00:40:25,520
I'm very observant.

582
00:40:26,622 --> 00:40:28,360
I can spot even the slightest thing that's off.

583
00:40:30,894 --> 00:40:32,781
And it's not just magicians I can see through.

584
00:40:35,576 --> 00:40:36,960
I can spot liars too.

585
00:40:41,251 --> 00:40:44,480
So what am I to you?

586
00:40:45,640 --> 00:40:46,760
A magician or a liar?

587
00:40:52,838 --> 00:40:54,560
If I can't see through you, you're a magician.

588
00:40:56,470 --> 00:40:57,471
But if I can,

589
00:40:59,579 --> 00:41:00,688
then you're a liar.

590
00:41:04,125 --> 00:41:06,320
People are always trying to figure out magic tricks.

591
00:41:07,470 --> 00:41:08,760
Don't take it so seriously.

592
00:41:10,462 --> 00:41:12,320
Just enjoy the show.

593
00:42:11,630 --> 00:42:13,480
Mommy Ta! Mommy Ta!

594
00:42:24,040 --> 00:42:27,880
Why did you call her that? Why?

595
00:42:41,534 --> 00:42:45,363
Hey, make sure you apologize to Mom first, okay?

596
00:42:46,535 --> 00:42:48,320
Will Mom apologize to me too?

597
00:42:49,531 --> 00:42:52,840
Of course. She knows she went too far.

598
00:42:54,704 --> 00:42:55,705
Ready?

599
00:42:57,000 --> 00:42:58,001
Let's go.

600
00:43:06,312 --> 00:43:08,179
Oh, you're back!

601
00:43:10,648 --> 00:43:11,926
How was it?

602
00:43:12,531 --> 00:43:16,160
Did my little adventurer have fun?

603
00:43:20,132 --> 00:43:21,133
Titus.

604
00:43:27,611 --> 00:43:28,612
Mom.

605
00:43:31,035 --> 00:43:32,036
I'm sorry.

606
00:43:34,395 --> 00:43:37,300
I won't run away from home again.

607
00:43:38,859 --> 00:43:41,443
I'll ask for permission before going anywhere.

608
00:43:45,552 --> 00:43:46,553
Good girl.

609
00:43:48,350 --> 00:43:50,080
I'll let you go wherever you want.

610
00:43:51,390 --> 00:43:53,075
Except to see that woman.

611
00:44:00,131 --> 00:44:01,960
Throw that away. I'll buy you a new one.

612
00:44:11,979 --> 00:44:14,720
You're so mean! You're cruel! I hate you!

613
00:44:14,774 --> 00:44:16,200
I hate you when you're like this!

614
00:44:16,246 --> 00:44:17,320
- Titus!
- Wait!

615
00:44:17,347 --> 00:44:19,904
Who taught you to talk like that? Was it that woman?

616
00:44:19,979 --> 00:44:21,960
She taught you that, didn't she? Didn't she?

617
00:44:22,315 --> 00:44:23,560
- She taught you that, didn't she?
- Napha, calm down!

618
00:44:23,606 --> 00:44:25,579
Calm down!

619
00:44:25,607 --> 00:44:26,718
You wicked mother!

620
00:44:27,500 --> 00:44:28,854
Titus! Titus!

621
00:44:29,000 --> 00:44:30,427
Why are you being so disrespectful?

622
00:44:30,598 --> 00:44:32,440
- Titus!
- Hey! Hey!

623
00:44:33,686 --> 00:44:34,687
I'll go check on her.

624
00:44:40,576 --> 00:44:41,577
Phop!

625
00:44:41,947 --> 00:44:44,758
That bitch has poisoned our daughter's mind and
turned her into a little monster!

626
00:44:44,832 --> 00:44:46,374
What are you going to do about it?

627
00:45:00,798 --> 00:45:02,424
- Hello?
- Hey!

628
00:45:03,139 --> 00:45:04,800
The fingerprint results are back.

629
00:45:05,120 --> 00:45:08,560
Good! Make several copies and keep them safe.

630
00:45:09,000 --> 00:45:10,240
That bitch Nopnapha is capable of anything.

631
00:45:10,336 --> 00:45:11,960
She might try to steal the evidence back.

632
00:45:12,187 --> 00:45:15,720
There's no trace of Nopnapha's fingerprints!

633
00:45:16,070 --> 00:45:18,071
What? None of her fingerprints?

634
00:45:18,272 --> 00:45:19,560
Then whose fingerprints are on it?

635
00:45:20,300 --> 00:45:23,480
Jenphop's. His are the only fingerprints on it.

636
00:45:23,707 --> 00:45:26,840
The phone belongs to Jenphop, not Nopnapha.

637
00:45:29,763 --> 00:45:31,564
Munin, are you listening?

638
00:45:34,764 --> 00:45:35,765
Munin!

639
00:45:36,290 --> 00:45:39,320
You've been going after the wrong person all along!

640
00:46:00,115 --> 00:46:03,120
Based on the evidence we have now, our prime suspect

641
00:46:03,160 --> 00:46:04,520
is Jenphop.

642
00:46:12,120 --> 00:46:14,040
The uncle and nephew might be working together.

643
00:46:14,179 --> 00:46:16,240
True. But I have someone else in mind

644
00:46:16,926 --> 00:46:19,127
who can give us inside information on Jenphop.

645
00:46:19,347 --> 00:46:20,348
Who?

646
00:46:22,512 --> 00:46:23,880
People are saying

647
00:46:24,533 --> 00:46:28,234
you are the most vicious mistress in history.

648
00:46:28,379 --> 00:46:33,280
I wonder who told the Minister about Ta's affair with the Director.

649
00:46:34,451 --> 00:46:35,720
It could be you, Hong.

650
00:46:36,520 --> 00:46:38,600
A legendary slap like this?

651
00:46:38,678 --> 00:46:40,440
I've got to see it up close!

652
00:46:43,840 --> 00:46:44,841
Don't tell me...
